# Testing And Evidence

Verification must match the risk and blast radius of the change.

## Required Evidence For Checkpoint-Weight Work

Write evidence under `develop/artifacts/**` with:

- input or trigger;
- scope and anti-scope;
- files changed;
- commands/checks run;
- results;
- reviewer or audit notes;
- missing regression checks;
- known gaps;
- next step.

## Verification Rules

- Run repo-native tests, lint, build or smoke commands when available.
- If a command cannot run, record the exact blocker and use the narrowest honest proof.
- Do not claim broad correctness from a narrow check.
- Do not hide warnings that affect the task.
- For UI work, capture browser or visual evidence when the UI is part of the claim.

## Readiness Evidence

Project onboarding evidence must include inspected files, files created/changed, interview answers, unresolved questions, readiness status and verification output.
